# Derived: 16 ranks x 16 threads on ONE node -- 256 threads on 128 cores, so
# both SMT siblings of every core are computing.  That is the geometry the run
# asked for, so nothing may fire.
#
# This is the guard on the occupancy threshold.  want_occ is derived as
# ceil(threads-on-this-node / cores-on-this-node): 1 for the usual 128-thread
# node, 2 here.  Hardcoding one thread per core would make every deliberate SMT
# run look oversubscribed and drop it from comparison.
